{"id":358578,"title":"DisenchantingForge","summary":"Disenchant items and move the enchantments to books","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"http://cf.way2muchnoise.eu/versions/358578.svg\" alt=\"Badge: Available-for\" height=\"25\"\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003cimg src=\"http://cf.way2muchnoise.eu/full_358578_downloads.svg\" alt=\"Badge: Downloads\" height=\"25\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eDisenchanting Forge\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis mod adds a Disenchanter block that will let you disenchant enchanted items and transfer their enchantments onto books. The Disenchanter will remove the first enchantment from the item and transfer it onto a book. If you shift-click the output book, the Disenchanter will try to transfer all enchantments onto all available books, assuming you have enough experience and books to cover the cost. You can use the random_enchantment config to pull a specific enchantment off an item by placing and re-placing it in the input slot until the desired enchanted book appears in the output. Actually choosing the enchantment is on the roadmap.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eFabric version: \u003cspan style=\"color:#36f\"\u003e\u003ca style=\"color:#36f\" href=\"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/disenchantingfabric\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eDisenchanting Fabric\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eHow to Use\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePut an enchanted item into the left slot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlace a book or stack of books into the middle slot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnchanted book will generate with the first enchantment from the enchanted item\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTaking the book will remove that enchantment from the item and give you the book\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eRecipe\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e1 Anvil\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e1 Enchantment table\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e2 Gold ingots\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e3 Obsidian\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://gitlab.com/chirptheboy/disenchanting/raw/master/web/recipe.png\" alt=\"Recipe\" width=\"572\" height=\"271\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eBlacklist\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTemplate:\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href=\"https://gitlab.com/chirptheboy/disenchanting/-/raw/master/DisenchantingBlacklist.zip?inline=false\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eDisenchantingBlacklist.zip\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTutorial: \u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgHWz8kuLPo\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UgHWz8kuLPo\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eConfig options\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003erequires_xp\u003c/span\u003e: Does disenchanting require experience?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003exp_cost\u003c/span\u003e: Relative scale (1 - 10) of how much XP the disenchanter costs to use (lower requires less XP)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003erandom_enchantment\u003c/span\u003e: When true, the disenchanter will pick a random enchantment from the item. Default value is false, which is existing behavior. Introduced in version 1.4.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003eresetAnvilCost\u003c/span\u003e: When true, the item's anvil work cost will be reset to zero. Defaults to false. Introduced in version 2.0.0.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003edamageItem\u003c/span\u003e: Should the enchanted item be damaged during the disenchanting process? Defaults to false. Introduced in version 2.1.0.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003edamagePercent\u003c/span\u003e: Percent of damage that should be done to the item on each disenchant. Defaults to 5. Introduced in version 2.1.0.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-family:\u0026amp;#x27\"\u003eshowInUseMessage\u003c/span\u003e: Show a message when the disenchanter is in use by another player.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease log bugs on the issue tracker \u003ca href=\"https://gitlab.com/chirptheboy/disenchanting/issues\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. Follow on Bluesky for updates \u003ca href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/chirptheboy.bsky.social\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eResource packs\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/texture-packs/excalibur-disenchantingforge-support\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eExcalibur\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://gitlab.com/chirptheboy/disenchanting/-/tree/master/packs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eBDCraft\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eModpack makers\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFeel free to include this in your modpacks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eSpecial thanks\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/McJtyMods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eMcJty\u003c/a\u003e for his Forge modding tutorial for 1.14\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Tsudico/Disenchanting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eTsudico\u003c/a\u003e for his Disenchanting mod for Fabric\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca hre